# {{.project_name}}

Multimodal AI testing project created with PromptArena.

## Overview

This project tests a model's vision capabilities with two starter scenarios:
- Image analysis and description
- Image comparison

Extend it with your own images for object detection, OCR, or visual question
answering.

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- PromptArena CLI installed
{{range .providers}}{{if eq . "mock"}}- Nothing else for the mock provider: it replays scripted replies from `mock-responses.yaml`, so the kit runs with no API key
{{else if eq . "openai"}}- OpenAI API access to a vision-capable model (GPT-4o family)
{{else if eq . "claude"}}- Anthropic API access to a vision-capable Claude model
{{else if eq . "gemini"}}- Google Gemini API access (vision enabled)
{{end}}{{end}}
### Setup

{{range .providers}}{{if eq . "openai"}}- Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` (in `.env` or your shell). Get a key from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
{{else if eq . "claude"}}- Set `CLAUDE_API_KEY` or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (in `.env` or your shell). Get a key from: https://console.anthropic.com/
{{else if eq . "gemini"}}- Set `GEMINI_API_KEY` (in `.env` or your shell). Get a key from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
{{end}}{{end}}
Run the tests:

```bash
promptarena run
```

