## Scenarios

### Image Analysis (`scenarios/image-analysis.scenario.yaml`)
Sends `media/red-square.png` and checks the model names the shape and colour
in a reasonably detailed description.

### Image Comparison (`scenarios/image-comparison.scenario.yaml`)
Sends `media/red-square.png` and `media/blue-circle.png` together and checks
the model compares them and identifies both shapes.
{{range .providers}}{{if eq . "mock"}}
### Mock replies (`mock-responses.yaml`)
The mock provider answers each scenario with the scripted reply keyed by the
scenario's `metadata.name`. The replies describe the shipped images, so the
kit passes offline. They prove the configuration and assertions are wired up,
not that any model can see; switch to a real provider for that.
{{end}}{{end}}
## Adding Your Own Images

Put the file in `media/` and reference it from a scenario turn. `file_path`
resolves relative to `config.arena.yaml`:

```yaml
turns:
  - role: user
    parts:
      - type: text
        text: "Describe this image."
      - type: image
        media:
          file_path: media/your-image.jpg
          mime_type: image/jpeg
```

A publicly reachable image can be referenced with `url:` in place of
`file_path:`, and a small image can be embedded as base64 with `data:`.
Local files keep the tests reproducible and offline.

## Customization

### Adding Specific Tests

Create custom scenarios for your use cases:

```yaml
# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://promptkit.altairalabs.ai/schemas/v1alpha1/scenario.json
apiVersion: promptkit.altairalabs.ai/v1alpha1
kind: Scenario
metadata:
  name: product-photos

spec:
  id: check-product-quality
  task_type: vision
  description: "Verify product photo quality"
  
  turns:
    - role: user
      parts:
        - type: text
          text: "Is this product photo suitable for e-commerce? Check lighting, focus, and composition."
        - type: image
          media:
            file_path: media/product.jpg
            mime_type: image/jpeg
      assertions:
        - type: contains_any
          params:
            patterns: ["lighting", "focus", "quality"]
```

## Running Tests

```bash
# Run all scenarios
promptarena run

# Run specific scenario
promptarena run --scenario image-analysis

# Run with specific provider
promptarena run --provider <provider-id>   # spec.id from providers/*.provider.yaml

# Use lower temperature for more consistent analysis
promptarena run --temperature 0.3
```

## Best Practices

### Image Quality
- Use high-resolution images (at least 512x512)
- Ensure good lighting and clarity
- Avoid overly compressed images

### Testing Strategy
- Test with diverse image types
- Include edge cases (low light, busy scenes, etc.)
- Verify consistent behavior across providers
- Test different image formats (JPEG, PNG, WebP)

### Assertions
- Verify key objects are identified
- Check for appropriate detail level
- Ensure factual accuracy
- Test for harmful content detection (if needed)

